 "method_notes": "Westminster community schools (summarised criteria in the 'Your choice for primary education 2027' brochure, matching the determined admission arrangements 2027/28): final criterion 'Children living nearest to the school calculated as a straight line measurement from the child's home \"address point\" determined by Ordnance Survey data to the main entrance of the school building used by pupils', using the Council's geographical measuring system. Brochure figures are 'of a mile'/'miles' and are the distance reached for the last offer on that criterion. Exceptions found: Millbank Gardens, Pimlico Primary (Future Academies), St Peter's Chippenham Mews and St Matthew's use shortest walking route; St Augustine's tie-break is by walking route; Soho Parish measures to the centre of the school grounds; Gateway Academy to its nearest pupil entrance; Ark King Solomon to the midpoint between its two sites' entrances; St John's Wood Primary to the Bridgeman Street main entrance; St Saviour's to its Shirland Road entrance. Many VA schools fill most places on faith criteria first.",
