 "gaps": "Most Westminster schools were undersubscribed ('all applicants offered'). Missing values: Wilberforce 2026 (no outcome in the 2027 brochure); St Peter's Chippenham Mews 2026 (the brochure text is garbled and has no figure) and 2024 (oversubscribed but no distance printed); St John's Wood Primary 2024 (school opened Sept 2025). Its predecessors Robinsfield Infant (all offered in 2024), George Eliot Primary (all offered in 2024) and Barrow Hill Junior (junior school), plus Our Lady of Dolours Catholic Primary (absent from the 2026 and 2027 brochures, so presumed closed), are left out. St Clement Danes 2026 has no distance: it was oversubscribed but filled on church categories. Faith-school figures are often the distance reached inside a faith category; see criterion_note. Units are as printed: 'of a mile' is recorded as miles. Brochure pages were parsed by text extraction, and the 2024 two-up spreads were checked against rendered images. The measuring method of VA schools whose summaries don't state one is assumed to be the council's straight-line default. PANs come from the 2027 brochure (Edward Wilson's was 56 in earlier years). Postcodes come from the brochure school pages, not checked against GIAS.",
